1. The tumor size is 5.5 cm in diameter, which falls within the T1 category. T1 tumors are 7 cm or less in greatest dimension, and are further divided into T1a (tumor 4 cm or less) and T1b (tumor more than 4 cm but not more than 7 cm). In this case, the tumor is more than 4 cm, so it is a T1b tumor.
2. The tumor is described as well-circumscribed, with a foci where it appears to extend through the renal capsule. However, there is no definitive evidence of invasion into the perirenal adipose tissue, renal sinus, major veins, ureter, or lymphovascular structures. The surgical margins are also negative.
3. Therefore, based on the AJCC Cancer Staging Manual (7th edition), the T stage for this Kidney Chromophobe cancer is T1b (pT1b pNx pMx).}
